    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d628">

                <pb facs="0760" n="672" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg672"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.5151/179: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-07-28T16:00:00-05:00">July 28, 1933—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>25. My despatch No. 1063, July 14.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d628-f1"/> I am informed
                    by the Foreign Office that an agreement has been reached to the effect that 50
                    percent of the exchange arising from future Ecuadorian exports to France <pb
                        facs="0761" n="673" xml:id="pg673"/> will be devoted to payment of sums due
                    French nationals. The negotiations have been conducted in Paris and further
                    details concerning arrangement are not yet available here.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d628-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d628-f1" n="1" xml:id="d628-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d628-f2" n="2" xml:id="d628-f2-content">
                <p>For text of the clearing agreement between Ecuador and France, signed July 27,
                    1933, see French <hi rendition="#italic">Journal Officiel</hi>, August 4, 1933,
                    p. 8287.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
